# Query keys and errors

- Every cache key comes from `lib/query-keys.ts` (`queryKeys.<entity>`) — never an inline array literal
  in a component or controller. Add new entities there, don't hand-roll a key next to the `useQuery` call.
- Controllers catch failures via `useMutation`'s `onError` (or a try/catch around a direct usecase call)
  and route them through `toastError`/`toastAppError` (`lib/toast-error.ts`) — never a bare
  `console.error` or a swallowed error.
- Need a load that shouldn't surface a toast (e.g. a background prefetch)? Add a `silent?: boolean` param
  to the controller function rather than special-casing error handling per call site.
